# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.db

# Windows resource files generated from cmd/kite-collector/app.manifest
# by `make windows-resources` (or the goreleaser before-hook). They embed
# the UAC manifest + Common-Controls 6.0 dependency into the .exe. Built
# artifact — regenerated from the .manifest source on every release.
*.syso

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Build output
bin/
# goreleaser + scripts/build-msi.sh output (dist/cache/ holds the pinned
# osquery MSI download for the --with-osquery bundle build)
dist/
*.msi

# Runtime data
data/

# Local dev PKI (mTLS agent identity + certs). Contains private keys —
# must never be committed; regenerate with the dev enrollment flow.
.kite-dev/

# Claude Code
.claude/
.claude-merge-tmp/
/kite-collector
/kite-collector.new
/kite-collector.release

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
internal/discovery/network/jsfingerprint/jsfingerprint_test.go
identity.json
cmd/kite-collector/web_fingerprint_test.go:

# Local-only e2e tests that hit real daemons/CLIs on the dev machine
# (build-tagged `e2e`, so go test ./... ignores them anyway, but we
# keep them out of git to avoid tying expectations to a specific host).
internal/discovery/agent/vpn/source_tailscale_e2e_test.go

# Ubuntu package-matrix run artifacts (RFC-0149). Each leg writes its result
# payload here; in CI the path is overridden by KITE_MATRIX_REPORT_DIR and the
# JSON is uploaded as a build artifact, never committed.
tests/e2e/ubuntu-matrix/.matrix-reports/
ubuntu-package-matrix-*.log
# Collector binaries are produced by CI and attached to releases. They must
# never be embedded in or committed to the source tree.
internal/dashboard/assets/kite-collector_windows_386_legacy.exe

# RFC-0156: the checksum-verified osqueryd payload scripts/stage-osquery-embed.sh
# stages into the go:embed tree for the self-contained Windows installer. ~55 MB
# of third-party build output, reproducible from scripts/osquery-pin.env — the
# pin is what is version-controlled, not the bytes. (osqueryd.exe is already
# covered by the *.exe rule above; these cover the rest of the staged tree.)
internal/installer/osquerypayload/payload/manifest.json
internal/installer/osquerypayload/payload/osquery/
